# Build artifacts from ti/build_ti.{ps1,sh} and the CMake stub build.
# The TI build drops a ~14 MB .out and a ~2 MB .map here; none of it belongs
# in history (the shippable image is signed and published under prebuilt/).
build/

# Cygwin/MSYS crash dumps.  The Windows bench shell drops these in the repo
# root and `git add -A` has swept them into history more than once.
*.stackdump
build-tests/
build-linux/
# CONTRIBUTING.md documents the stub build as build/stub (covered by build/
# above), but any hyphenated build-<name>/ dir (build-stub/, build-spi/,
# build-sdio/, ...) is the same easy slip -- a literal build-stub/ rule
# already missed build-spi/ and build-sdio/ once.  Cover the whole family.
build*/

# Binary firmware images.  prebuilt/.gitignore re-includes `cc3501e-*.bin`
# because the signed prebuilt images shipped there ARE committed -- but that
# re-include was written against a root `*.bin` rule that did not exist, so it
# re-included nothing and every OTHER .bin in the tree stayed stageable.
*.bin

# The staged OTA self-test candidate: a bin2c C array of a SIGNED TI GPE vendor
# image, internal-class per the project's public/internal split (alp-sdk#590).
# hal/ti/cc3501e_ota_candidate.README.md tells developers to copy it in here and
# said it was git-ignored -- it was NOT, so following that README and then
# running `git add -A` would commit a license-gated signed firmware blob into
# this PUBLIC repository, and a history rewrite is the only remedy.
hal/ti/cc3501e_ota_candidate.c

# The TI SimpleLink CC33xx SDK is NOT redistributable.
# vendor/simplelink-cc33xx/README.md documents this path as git-ignored.
vendor/simplelink-cc33xx/sdk/
